WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.285 --> 00:00:04.392
- What's up, Believe Nations?

00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:06.470
Greetings from Copenhagen, Denmark.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.558
My name is Evan, my one word is believe

00:00:08.558 --> 00:00:09.961
and I believe in people

00:00:09.961 --> 00:00:11.112
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:11.112 --> 00:00:13.573
And, my hope is that a little
bit of that rubs off onto you

00:00:13.573 --> 00:00:16.462
so you can create something
amazing in this world.

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:18.496
So, to help you on your journey,
today we're going to look

00:00:18.496 --> 00:00:22.185
at five lessons in life that
people often learn too late,

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:25.505
and hopefully you can
pick it up a lot sooner.

00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:29.865
Lesson number one is don't
sleepwalk through life.

00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:33.797
- I advise students, as much
as possible, look for the job

00:00:33.797 --> 00:00:36.245
that you would take, if
you didn't need a job.

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:38.765
I mean, don't sleepwalk through life,

00:00:38.765 --> 00:00:41.474
and don't says it's all
going to be great, you know,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.453
I'll do this and I'll do that, you know,

00:00:43.453 --> 00:00:45.405
I'm just marking time for it to be older.

00:00:45.405 --> 00:00:47.324
I've told people, that's
like saving up sex

00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:48.908
for your old age.

00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:49.911
It just is not,

00:00:49.911 --> 00:00:52.143
it is not a good idea.

00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:55.476
(laughing and clapping)

00:01:01.438 --> 00:01:02.834
- What are you urging them to do?

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:06.417
- I'll explain just
what I'm talking about.

00:01:12.335 --> 00:01:16.252
You really want to be
doing, what you love doing.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.608
And, you can't necessarily
find it on your first job.

00:01:19.608 --> 00:01:21.806
But, don't give up before you find it.

00:01:21.806 --> 00:01:25.242
- Lesson number two,
live life without fear.

00:01:25.242 --> 00:01:27.409
- If there was one concept

00:01:29.307 --> 00:01:31.807
that I would suggest to people

00:01:33.096 --> 00:01:36.763
to take a daily
confrontation with, is fear.

00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:41.585
The problem with fear, is that it lies.

00:01:42.508 --> 00:01:45.925
Right, so, fear tells you, hey, you know,

00:01:46.891 --> 00:01:50.773
if you say that to that girl,
she's going to know she has you.

00:01:50.773 --> 00:01:51.606
You know.

00:01:51.606 --> 00:01:54.754
And she'll never really
be attracted to you,

00:01:54.754 --> 00:01:57.257
if she knows how much
you attracted to her.

00:01:57.257 --> 00:01:58.459
(laughing)

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:00.725
Don't say that, no, how we get her

00:02:00.725 --> 00:02:03.254
is when she walks by, ignore her.

00:02:03.254 --> 00:02:05.557
(laughing)

00:02:05.557 --> 00:02:07.172
- This little puppet on your shoulder.

00:02:07.172 --> 00:02:10.255
Fear tells you dumb like that, right?

00:02:11.582 --> 00:02:12.665
You know, so,

00:02:13.705 --> 00:02:17.122
for me, the daily confrontation with fear

00:02:19.185 --> 00:02:20.868
has become a real practice for me

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.829
since about three years ago,

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:25.996
I went skydiving in Dubai.

00:02:28.085 --> 00:02:30.835
Skydiving is a really interesting

00:02:31.692 --> 00:02:34.541
confront with fear, right?

00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:38.438
I got to stand up, I got to
stand up, I got to stand up.

00:02:38.438 --> 00:02:41.252
So, all your friends,
what happens is go out,

00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:43.563
how you, oh sorry, I dropped my thing.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:46.497
So what happens is, you
go out the night before,

00:02:46.497 --> 00:02:49.133
and you take a drink with your friends,

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.628
and somebody says, yeah, we
should go skydiving tomorrow.

00:02:51.628 --> 00:02:52.669
(laughing)

00:02:52.669 --> 00:02:54.541
And you go, yeah, we'll
go skydiving tomorrow.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:59.040
Yeah, yeah, and you go yeah,
and everybody goes yeah, right?

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.334
And you go home, you by
yourself, you like, hmm.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:04.160
(laughing)

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.223
You like, well, yeah, I
mean, they was drunk, too.

00:03:07.223 --> 00:03:08.306
(laughing)

00:03:08.306 --> 00:03:13.006
- Right, so, maybe, maybe
they not, we don't have to go,

00:03:13.006 --> 00:03:14.694
we don't have to do it.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.439
So then, that night,
you're laying in your bed,

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:18.544
and you just keep, (startles),

00:03:18.544 --> 00:03:19.377
(laughing)

00:03:19.377 --> 00:03:22.143
and you're terrified, you keep
imaginin' over and over again

00:03:22.143 --> 00:03:24.831
jumping out of an airplane,
and you can't figure out

00:03:24.831 --> 00:03:27.153
why you would do that, right?

00:03:27.153 --> 00:03:29.694
And, you're laying there, you
have the worst night's sleep

00:03:29.694 --> 00:03:31.974
of your life, but you still
have the hope that your friends

00:03:31.974 --> 00:03:33.038
were drunk, right?

00:03:33.038 --> 00:03:34.261
(laughing)

00:03:34.261 --> 00:03:36.647
So, you wake up the next day,
and you go, you know, down,

00:03:36.647 --> 00:03:38.087
and you said where you were going to meet,

00:03:38.087 --> 00:03:39.760
and everybody's there.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.766
And you're like, aw, um, all
right, all right, cool, cool,

00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:45.631
cool, cool, cool, cool, right?

00:03:45.631 --> 00:03:48.954
So, you get in the van, and you
don't know that your friends

00:03:48.954 --> 00:03:51.501
had the same night that you
had, 'cause they're pretending

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.387
like they didn't, they're like, yeah man,

00:03:53.387 --> 00:03:55.881
my uncle's a Navy Seal, and
you know, this is going to be

00:03:55.881 --> 00:03:57.501
great, I been looking forward to this.

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.916
And, you like, oh my God, oh my God.

00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:02.715
And your stomach is terrible,
you can't eat, and everything

00:04:02.715 --> 00:04:04.766
but you don't want to be the only punk,

00:04:04.766 --> 00:04:07.147
who doesn't jump out of this airplane.

00:04:07.147 --> 00:04:10.800
So, you get there, and then
you have this safety brief,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.487
and you're standing there
and the guys are telling you

00:04:12.487 --> 00:04:13.956
well, if the chute doesn't
open, what's going to happen

00:04:13.956 --> 00:04:16.744
is you do--well why the
hell, what could happen,

00:04:16.744 --> 00:04:17.740
(laughing)

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.187
that the chute wouldn't open, right?

00:04:20.187 --> 00:04:22.229
So you do a thing, and what
you do is your first jump,

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:25.282
you're attached to a guy, who, you know,

00:04:25.282 --> 00:04:26.387
he's going to walk you out.

00:04:26.387 --> 00:04:29.700
So, you go, and you get
there and there's an airplane

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.182
and nobody's stopping.

00:04:31.182 --> 00:04:33.270
Everybody's still going.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.819
So, you get onto the airplane,
and you're sitting there,

00:04:35.819 --> 00:04:37.852
and, you know, it's extra
because you're sitting

00:04:37.852 --> 00:04:40.246
on some dude's lap, some stranger.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:41.242
(laughing)

00:04:41.242 --> 00:04:42.607
You sitting on his lap,
and it's like, you know,

00:04:42.607 --> 00:04:45.515
you trying to make small talk, yeah man,

00:04:45.515 --> 00:04:47.117
(laughing)

00:04:47.117 --> 00:04:50.175
So, the deal, you be jumping
with people all the time, huh?

00:04:50.175 --> 00:04:52.225
(laughing)

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.240
Right, you know,

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.619
so, and then you just want
to make sure, you got kids,

00:04:55.619 --> 00:04:58.335
you know, you got people
you need to see, right?

00:04:58.335 --> 00:04:59.767
You just want to make
sure he's serious, right?

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:01.539
You get in there, so everything is normal,

00:05:01.539 --> 00:05:04.295
so you fly, you go up,
you go up, you go up,

00:05:04.295 --> 00:05:08.170
you go up to 14,000 feet, and
you notice there's a light,

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.373
it's red and it's yellow and green, right?

00:05:11.373 --> 00:05:13.422
So, right now, the light's red.

00:05:13.422 --> 00:05:15.126
So, then you start thinking, at some point

00:05:15.126 --> 00:05:16.985
the light's going to go
green, but you don't know

00:05:16.985 --> 00:05:19.176
what's going to happen, right?

00:05:19.176 --> 00:05:22.306
And you wait and it goes yellow,
and the light goes green,

00:05:22.306 --> 00:05:23.731
and somebody opens the door,

00:05:23.731 --> 00:05:25.645
and in that moment, you
realize you've never been

00:05:25.645 --> 00:05:28.292
in a frickin' airplane with the door open.

00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:30.765
(laughing)

00:05:30.765 --> 00:05:33.932
Right, terror, oh sorry, I'm spittin',

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:35.892
(spitting)

00:05:35.892 --> 00:05:40.122
oh, sorry, terror, terror,
terror, terror, terror, right?

00:05:40.122 --> 00:05:43.367
So, you go, and then, you know,

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.920
if you were smart, you sat in the back

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.450
so you don't go first, right?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.650
And then people start
going out of the airplane.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.817
And you go, and the guy walks
you up to the end of the thing

00:05:56.037 --> 00:05:59.324
and you're standing, and
you're toes are on the edge,

00:05:59.324 --> 00:06:02.574
and you're looking out, down, to death.

00:06:03.622 --> 00:06:05.619
(laughing)

00:06:05.619 --> 00:06:07.554
And they say, on three.

00:06:07.554 --> 00:06:11.126
And they say one, two,
and he pushes you on two,

00:06:11.126 --> 00:06:13.654
because people grab on three, right?

00:06:13.654 --> 00:06:16.142
(laughing)

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:20.091
And you go, (inhaling),

00:06:20.091 --> 00:06:22.197
and you fall out of the airplane,

00:06:22.197 --> 00:06:24.697
and in one second, you realize

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:29.957
that it's the most blissful
experience of your life,

00:06:31.137 --> 00:06:32.969
you're flying, right?

00:06:32.969 --> 00:06:35.370
It doesn't feel like
falling, right, it's like,

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:39.156
you actually are kind of held
a little bit, by the wind.

00:06:39.156 --> 00:06:41.984
And then you start, you start
falling, you're falling,

00:06:41.984 --> 00:06:44.017
there's zero fear.

00:06:44.017 --> 00:06:47.644
You realize that the
point of maximum danger

00:06:47.644 --> 00:06:50.612
is the point of minimum fear.

00:06:50.612 --> 00:06:52.529
It's bliss, it's bliss.

00:06:53.529 --> 00:06:57.911
And you're flying,
(nervous laughing) right,

00:06:57.911 --> 00:07:02.257
and you're doing it, and
then, 20 seconds, 25 seconds,

00:07:02.257 --> 00:07:05.343
40 seconds, and you have enough
time to just kind of be like,

00:07:05.343 --> 00:07:08.926
aw, that's that building
I saw right there,

00:07:10.047 --> 00:07:11.788
oh, you can see the ocean.

00:07:11.788 --> 00:07:12.911
(laughing)

00:07:12.911 --> 00:07:14.498
Right, you start doing all of that

00:07:14.498 --> 00:07:16.403
and the lesson for me was,

00:07:16.403 --> 00:07:19.807
why were you scared in
your bed the night before?

00:07:19.807 --> 00:07:22.431
Why did you, what do
you need that fear for?

00:07:22.431 --> 00:07:23.577
Just don't go.

00:07:23.577 --> 00:07:28.352
Why are you scared in your
bed, 16 hours before you jump?

00:07:28.352 --> 00:07:30.792
Why are you scared in the car?

00:07:30.792 --> 00:07:33.677
Why could you not enjoy breakfast?

00:07:33.677 --> 00:07:35.510
What did you need that,

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:36.926
the fear is,

00:07:36.926 --> 00:07:38.009
fear of what?

00:07:38.865 --> 00:07:40.796
You're nowhere even near the airplane.

00:07:40.796 --> 00:07:43.862
Everything up to the stepping out,

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:47.355
there's actually no reason to be scared.

00:07:47.355 --> 00:07:49.982
It only just ruins your day.

00:07:49.982 --> 00:07:51.720
You don't have to jump.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:54.396
And then, in that moment, all of a sudden,

00:07:54.396 --> 00:07:57.289
when you should be terrified,
is the most blissful

00:07:57.289 --> 00:07:59.135
experience of your life.

00:07:59.135 --> 00:08:03.128
And, God placed the best things in life,

00:08:03.128 --> 00:08:05.484
on the other side of terror,

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:07.528
on the other side of your maximum fear

00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:10.046
are all of the best things in life.

00:08:10.046 --> 00:08:13.664
- Lesson number three, stop complaining.

00:08:13.664 --> 00:08:16.032
- What if I told you this
is the last Monday morning

00:08:16.032 --> 00:08:17.039
of your life?

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:18.586
What if I told you, you die this week?

00:08:18.586 --> 00:08:20.611
Would you complain about your crap job,

00:08:20.611 --> 00:08:22.259
or that test you don't want to take?

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:23.652
I doubt it.

00:08:23.652 --> 00:08:25.972
You would go much higher level thinking.

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:27.470
Well, that's really what it takes.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:30.456
It takes understanding
that if you're not pumped,

00:08:30.456 --> 00:08:33.327
right now, if you're begrudging
what you're about to do,

00:08:33.327 --> 00:08:35.223
if you're not looking forward to it.

00:08:35.223 --> 00:08:37.087
Look, I respect practicality.

00:08:37.087 --> 00:08:39.616
You got to go through school
'cause your parents want to,

00:08:39.616 --> 00:08:42.512
you got to pay your rent, you
got student loans, I get it.

00:08:42.512 --> 00:08:45.123
But please recognize the
world we're living in.

00:08:45.123 --> 00:08:46.526
We're living in a world where

00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:48.246
there's so much more
opportunity, this internet thing

00:08:48.246 --> 00:08:52.520
created way more opportunity
for all of us. Way more.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.337
I mean look, you might not even be alive,

00:08:54.337 --> 00:08:57.197
like, you're Mom and Dad could
have had sex, like three minutes

00:08:57.197 --> 00:08:59.231
later and you wouldn't even exist.

00:08:59.231 --> 00:09:00.564
And you're complaining.

00:09:00.564 --> 00:09:02.739
You could have ended
up being a bus, a tree.

00:09:02.739 --> 00:09:06.491
I just don't get the mentality
of being head down sad,

00:09:06.491 --> 00:09:07.844
on a Monday morning.

00:09:07.844 --> 00:09:09.572
I'm going to make Monday morning my.

00:09:09.572 --> 00:09:12.172
I'm going to make you
Saturday, Monday morning.

00:09:12.172 --> 00:09:13.683
That's what I want to do every morning,

00:09:13.683 --> 00:09:15.123
and that's what I want from you.

00:09:15.123 --> 00:09:18.229
Please, take a step back
and think about how awesome

00:09:18.229 --> 00:09:19.883
it actually is.

00:09:19.883 --> 00:09:22.321
And then, recognize that
you can attack the world,

00:09:22.321 --> 00:09:25.380
in a totally different way,
'cause you were lucky enough

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.630
to be born during this era.

00:09:28.755 --> 00:09:32.238
- Lesson number four,
know your destination.

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:35.505
- Imagine we're standing
in a big empty room, right?

00:09:35.505 --> 00:09:38.060
And, we're standing in
one corner, and I give you

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.868
a simple instruction.

00:09:39.868 --> 00:09:43.827
I want you to go to that corner,
in a straight line, right?

00:09:43.827 --> 00:09:46.203
Off you go, no big deal, right?

00:09:46.203 --> 00:09:48.848
Without telling you, I slip
a chair in front of you.

00:09:48.848 --> 00:09:50.061
What do you do?

00:09:50.061 --> 00:09:51.779
You go around the chair.

00:09:51.779 --> 00:09:53.563
Now, you just disobeyed
what I told you to do,

00:09:53.563 --> 00:09:56.118
I told you to go to that
corner straight line.

00:09:56.118 --> 00:09:57.770
But this is the amazing
things about human beings,

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:59.655
which is when we're given
a clear destination,

00:09:59.655 --> 00:10:03.214
we use our own creativity and
our own sense of innovation

00:10:03.214 --> 00:10:04.845
and our own problem solving abilities

00:10:04.845 --> 00:10:07.173
to overcome obstacles to
get to the destination.

00:10:07.173 --> 00:10:08.774
In other words, the
destination is more important

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:10.584
than the route, right?

00:10:10.584 --> 00:10:12.124
We are flexible about the route.

00:10:12.124 --> 00:10:14.228
We are obsessed with
the destination, reset.

00:10:14.228 --> 00:10:15.874
We're standing in the corner
together and I give you

00:10:15.874 --> 00:10:16.957
a simple instruction,

00:10:16.957 --> 00:10:18.248
go somewhere in this room

00:10:18.248 --> 00:10:19.652
in a straight line.

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:20.915
And you say to me, well
where do you want me to go?

00:10:20.915 --> 00:10:22.932
I'm like I dunno, you're
smart, figure it out.

00:10:22.932 --> 00:10:24.179
Go in a straight line.

00:10:24.179 --> 00:10:26.060
And so you pick a point
and you start walking,

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.720
and without telling you I
put a chair in front of you.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:28.754
And what do you do?

00:10:28.754 --> 00:10:30.103
You come to a grinding halt.

00:10:30.103 --> 00:10:31.111
I say, what'd you stop for?

00:10:31.111 --> 00:10:32.771
Well, you put a chair in front of me.

00:10:32.771 --> 00:10:37.185
Or, you'll make a sudden turn
and go in another direction.

00:10:37.185 --> 00:10:39.632
And this is the problem,
it's the same obstacle.

00:10:39.632 --> 00:10:41.888
The difference is when you
have a clear destination,

00:10:41.888 --> 00:10:44.283
the obstacles become easy to overcome,

00:10:44.283 --> 00:10:45.649
when you don't have a clear destination,

00:10:45.649 --> 00:10:47.159
you keep coming to a grinding halt

00:10:47.159 --> 00:10:48.548
and what we do in our companies,

00:10:48.548 --> 00:10:50.574
is we're counting the steps
we're taking along the route,

00:10:50.574 --> 00:10:52.662
but we're never looking
at the destination, right?

00:10:52.662 --> 00:10:55.234
So a company says, made
million dollars this year,

00:10:55.234 --> 00:10:57.097
we we're only planning on making $800,000.

00:10:57.097 --> 00:10:58.073
It's like, we took ten
steps, we were only planning

00:10:58.073 --> 00:10:59.235
on taking eight.

00:10:59.235 --> 00:11:00.159
Where you going?

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:01.250
No clue, right?

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:02.941
(laughing)

00:11:02.941 --> 00:11:03.918
We count the steps.

00:11:03.918 --> 00:11:05.620
And, so the point is, is
that people want to feel

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:06.836
that the effort they're exerting

00:11:06.836 --> 00:11:08.364
actually are moving somewhere.

00:11:08.364 --> 00:11:10.969
And so, successful measurement,
successful recognition.

00:11:10.969 --> 00:11:12.964
